    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Spoofed Header BEC", "technique": "T1566.001", "what_happened": "At 2030-08-27 09:14:02 UTC, mx01.corp.com Wazuh email-decoder captured inbound .eml with mismatched headers: From='CFO <cfo@corp.com>', Sender='alerts@external-domain.example', Reply-To='finance.urgent@protonmail.com', Return-Path='<bounce@external-domain.example>'. Message-ID '<p95-spoof-test@external-domain.example>' subject 'URGENT: confidential wire request - acquisition closing'. Source IP=45.227.255.190.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 95100 'Spoofed email header mismatch detected' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1566.001. From-domain≠Sender-domain≠Reply-To-domain≠Return-Path-domain (3 mismatches)."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Defense Evasion / Weak Auth on Spoofed Domain", "technique": "context", "what_happened": "DNS TXT lookups during ingestion: corp.com SPF='v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all', _dmarc.corp.com='v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:dmarc-rua@corp.com'. DMARC policy p=none = monitor-only (does NOT reject mismatch). DKIM signature on the message: NO dkim-signature header present.", "chain_reason": "Spoofed domain (corp.com) has DMARC p=none — header impersonation is technically permitted by policy gate. Attacker exploited this."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Impact / BEC Body Markers", "technique": "T1656", "what_happened": "Body content analysis hit all three BEC markers: urgency='URGENT'+'TODAY'+'closing meeting'; wire='EUR 250,000 wired'+'acquisition account'; secrecy='confidential — don't discuss with anyone, including the CEO'+'I can't talk now'. BEC score 3/3.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 95101 'BEC body markers: urgency+wire+secrecy' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1656."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Command and Control / Free-Mail Reply Channel", "technique": "T1102", "what_happened": "Reply-To header 'finance.urgent@protonmail.com' — free-mail provider, NOT a corp domain. Pattern: response to reply would land in attacker-controlled webmail inbox.", "chain_reason": "Reply-To→free-mail is the canonical BEC reply-channel hijack. Combined with From=cfo@corp.com, makes any reply land at attacker."}
